// Docket's tickets (tickets-patterns syntax.tex, Policy). coordd supplies these facts when it asks about tickets:
// each ticket asked about, who its step awaits, and how many minutes the step has been silent (asked every minute):
// WAITED is 0 while the awaited agent is in a turn or a runner job runs for the ticket, otherwise the minutes since the
// latest of the step being given, the agent's last turn end and the ticket's last job end (coordd ticket/quiet.rs).
// A step given to the runner is not silent while the project's source sees the runner alive; from when it is seen
// gone, it is.
// A wait lasts while the awaited process lives.
Fact ticket Identified by String
Fact awaits Identified by ticket * agent
Fact waited Identified by ticket * Int

// Naming an agent on a ticket: the names of a note or a post (coord msg NAME, --re, --thread, @NAME), which reach
// them at once. Anyone may name anyone, except a consultant, whose words are advice its members do not answer: a lead
// or a consultant may name one, and anyone may on a ticket the consultant takes part in already (someone brought it
// in). TAKES-PART is supplied by coordd: the ticket's opener, its posts' authors and those they named, whoever was
// given a delivery of it, and whoever works on it (`coord item start`: an item's starters, I-1480, N-1481 p15). So a
// consultant who started an item may be named on it by anyone. A new note is asked as a ticket nobody takes part in.
Fact takes-part Identified by agent * ticket
Act name
  Actor agent
  Recipient agent
  Related to ticket
  Holds when not role(recipient, "consultant")
  Holds when role(actor, "lead")
  Holds when role(actor, "consultant")
  Holds when takes-part(recipient, ticket)

// When a step has been silent too long it is withdrawn and the ticket fails where it stood (Silent), so the failure goes
// up the tree instead of the ticket waiting for ever. A step that waits on the owner does not expire: the owner is
// the last rung, with no one above to raise to. Nor does one on a ticket the owner archived (below): it is held, not
// silent, and comes again if he unarchives it. SILENT-AFTER is how long the step may be silent in minutes (WAITED,
// above: not its age; asked every minute); a project
// may shorten it with its own instance (`+silent-after(2).`): the shortest one given holds.
Fact silent-after Identified by Int
+silent-after(120).

// How many turns of an agent its own program's `every e.every of turn_end(e)` binding counts before it fires (the
// brain, N-1444 p16). A project sets it per agent, `+check-in-every("paper-research", 20).` (policy/agents/NAME.eflint),
// and he edits it there; coordd reads it as written (coordd policy/parts.rs) into each `turn_end` of that agent, so the
// record holds it. An agent with none has nothing fire.
Fact check-in-every Identified by agent * Int

// How far before the owner's burst, in seconds, the brain's attention pass reads his posts to the agent that it has
// not answered (the ledger, docket-machine `Machine::asked`; coordd brain.rs; the selector's candidates `unanswered by
// it`; proto-reader N-1446 p98, proto-lead p138). A project gives it in its own policy, `+unanswered-within(43200).`,
// and he edits it there; the shortest instance holds. With none, the pass reads none of them.
Fact unanswered-within Identified by Int

// How far before the owner's burst, in seconds, the brain's attention pass reads his earlier posts as an index (id,
// thread, time, first line): those on the burst's thread, the thread it hangs from and the threads hanging from it,
// and those to the agent (coordd brain.rs EARLIER; his repeats, paper-research-brain N-1449; proto-mind N-1446 p450).
// The owner model names the ones whose words on his topic the agent must have before it answers, and coordd adds those
// words, as he wrote them, to what the pass says. A project gives it in its own policy, `+earlier-within(604800).`, and
// he edits it there; the shortest instance holds. With none, the pass reads none of them.
Fact earlier-within Identified by Int

// How many of those posts the index lists, the newest (coordd brain.rs EARLIER): `+earlier-lines(100).`, the smallest
// instance holds; with none, 40. On research's record against paper-research-brain's lessons, it is this number, not
// the reach, that bounds what the owner model sees of what he had said before (proto-mind N-1446, I-1455).
Fact earlier-lines Identified by Int

// How far back, in seconds, the owner model reads his posts when it is built whole (owner_model.kind, coordd brain.rs
// `owner_model_env`; paper-research N-1446 p1108): from that long before the newest of the posts its update names. A
// project gives it in its own policy, as `+owner-model-within(604800).`; the shortest instance holds. With none, coordd
// opens no update, and no model is made.
Fact owner-model-within Identified by Int

// After how many misses since it was last built whole the owner model is built whole again rather than brought up to
// date (owner_model.kind's `owner_update`; the misses are the brain's predictions of his next words that his words did
// not bear out). `+owner-model-rebuild-after(3).`, the smallest instance holds; with none, as with no
// owner-model-within, coordd opens no update.
Fact owner-model-rebuild-after Identified by Int

Act expired
  Actor agent
  Related to ticket
  Holds when awaits(ticket, actor) and waited(ticket) >= silent-after() and actor != "owner" and not archived(ticket)

// A ticket's kind and opener, and the agents running now (supplied when a ticket's step asks who fills a role).
Fact ticket-kind Identified by ticket * String
Fact opener Identified by ticket * agent
Fact running Identified by agent
// Agent A works on item I (`coord item start`, the `started` line), for each open item: for example
// `Requires started(option, ctx.item)` gives a ticket under an item to whoever took the item.
Fact started Identified by agent * String

// A goal (`goal NAME` on a kind; Owed) is the act of that name, asked for the ticket's opener when its program
// returns: the ticket closes done only if it holds. coordd supplies what closed below the ticket: CLOSED-UNDER(T, KIND,
// HEAD), HEAD the result's constructor or the exception raised. For example a project's
//   Act green
//     Actor agent
//     Related to ticket
//     Holds when closed-under(ticket, "check", "Green")
Fact closed-under Identified by String * String * String

// Who else an event on a ticket reaches (syntax.tex, notify): besides whom a post names and whoever acts next, and
// besides the opener of a ticket that closes with no parent waiting. EVENT is "post" or "closed"; the actor is who
// caused it. coordd asks it for every agent and the owner. agent-base declares it, with `inform`, in notify.eflint
// (who hears of a post on a thread); a project replaces that file with its own policy/notify.eflint (an act is
// declared once). Without the act, nobody more is told. For example, "always tell the lead of a post on a claim":
//   Act notify
//     Actor agent
//     Recipient agent
//     Related to ticket, event
//     Holds when event == "post" and ticket-kind(ticket, "claim") and role(recipient, "lead")
// An act `inform`, declared the same way, tells whom it names without starting a turn for it: the notice is there at
// the recipient's next turn (plan/design-two-systems.md, section 10). Whom both name is notified.
Fact event Identified by String
// On a "closed" notice: the ticket closed with a raise (failed, cancelled, or given up at a stop), not done.
Fact closed-failed Identified by ticket

// Who may change a ticket (syntax.tex, `may edit`): cancel it, withdraw its step. Its opener (for a ticket opened by
// a pattern, the nearest opener above it), an agent above the opener in the agent tree, or a lead. The owner always
// may. ABOVE is supplied by coordd: A is above B when B's parent, or its parent's, and so on, is A.
Fact above Identified by agent * agent
Act edit
  Actor agent
  Related to ticket
  Holds when opener(ticket, actor)
  Holds when above(actor, opener(ticket))
  Holds when role(actor, "lead")

// What the owner archived (the owner, N-1073: "some relation in the eflint code that express this is no longer of
// importance to the owner ie archived"): ARCHIVED(T), supplied by coordd for a ticket he archived and for each ticket
// under it, worked out from the record's `archive` lines and kept nowhere else. It is made and unmade by his act alone
// (the window's Archive, `coord archive T`, `coord unarchive T`): the engine takes it from nobody else, whatever is
// written here. His own post on it unarchives it, as writing there says it matters to him again. It is not an end:
// nothing is closed, taken back or removed, and Unarchive puts it back as it was.
// What it asks of the agents, the library's: nobody is asked on it. The engine hands nothing at or under it while it
// is archived (a step, a post's wake, words given), puts its hole to no minder, and keeps what it holds, to hand it at
// Unarchive as it would have been; a held step does not expire (`expired`, above); and whoever holds work under it
// is told once, quietly (notify.eflint's `inform`, event "archived"). WORKS-UNDER(A, T), supplied with that event: A
// is awaited by a step at or under T, or opened an open ticket under it; never the owner.
Fact archived Identified by ticket
Fact works-under Identified by agent * ticket

// Who fills a role for a ticket's step (`step role R`; the call gives `role`, `call` and `ticket`): a running agent
// with that role. The call gives too the step's arguments that are texts, numbers or truths, each by its name
// (`call.by`), and each text of a list argument is among(X, I), I from 0 (paper-research N-1446 p2894: who reads a
// text change turns on who made it and what it touches).
Decision fills
  Options agent
  Requires role(option, call.role)
  Requires running(option)

// Where the open tickets stand, supplied when coordd asks a `when D is o` binding's decision D (beside its call fields,
// docket-machine `when_asks`; `Machine::standing`): STANDS(T, CALL), ticket T's program waits at a step or a hold of
// CALL now (`cut_of`; `decide:green` while a decision is asked); STANDS-WITH(T, PARAM, VALUE), that step's argument
// PARAM is the string VALUE (a commit); HANDS-IN(T, POST, BY), T's form's `for` names POST, or an item whose note POST
// is (the ASKED ledger's hand-in), which BY wrote (`owner` for his). Not declared here: a project that reads them
// declares them in its own policy (`Fact stands Identified by String * String`, `Fact stands-with Identified by String
// * String * String`, `Fact hands-in Identified by String * String * String`), so a release from before them, which
// supplies none, still loads it, and coordd supplies only what a policy declares.
